On 6/18/07, Turniansky, Michael [UNK] <MICHAEL.A.TURNIANSKY@saic.com> wrote:
> Not even in names.  You always need to put a "y" (or in names, at least
> a comma) between two of the same letters.

A comma wouldn't help either. (In fact, commas are always optional,
and don't really ever change anything.)

Double consonants are disallowed just like voiced-unvoiced clusters,
or "sc", "zj", etc.

